      "id": 1,
      "text": "Elizabeth began in 1855 as a saw‑mill camp along Running Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://smalltownvibe.org/elizabeth-co/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Denver & New Orleans Railroad arrived in 1882, turning the quiet settlement into a bustling hub for farming and ranching.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicelizabethco.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1882 Section House was restored in 2002 with a State Historical Fund grant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicelizabethco.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1998 Elizabeth adopted a preservation ordinance and created a Historic Advisory Board that helped list the Huber‑Carlson Building on the State Register in 1995.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicelizabethco.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Elizabeth’s historic downtown still hosts businesses in restored buildings, including a former brewery now home to a local brewery and a hat company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicelizabethco.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 2023 the First National Bank at 188 S Main St was added to the National Register of Historic Places, underscoring the town’s heritage focus.",
